<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Paduka Batara</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">died 1417</span></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Paduka Batara was a ruler of Sulu, in the southern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/philippines">Philippines</a>, who led a large embassy to the Ming court of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yongle-emperor">Yongle Emperor</a> in 1417. He fell ill and died at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dezhou">Dezhou</a> in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/shandong">Shandong</a> on the journey home and was buried there with imperial honours. His tomb survives, and some of his descendants settled in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/china">China</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/paduka-batara.jpg" alt="Paduka Batara" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Suginami · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:%E5%BE%B7%E5%B7%9E%E8%8B%8F%E7%A6%84%E7%8E%8B%E5%A2%93.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
